  scenarioId: EXP-03
  title: Citric Acid + Calcium Carbonate
  chemicalAId: CH-03
  chemicalBId: CH-10
  fixedConcentrationA: 0.10 M
  fixedQuantityA: 15 mL
  fixedConcentrationB: Suspension
  fixedQuantityB: 10 mL
  fixedConditions: 15 mL 0.10 M Citric Acid + 10 mL CaCO3 suspension, open beaker,
    ambient 22 C.
  reviewedRiskCategory: 1
  reviewStatus: 1
  reviewEvidence: X13-REV-2026-03
  dataVersion: 1.0.0
  controls:
  - Open vessel
  - Eye protection
  rationale: Mild organic acid reacting slowly with insoluble carbonate salt.
  observations: Gentle effervescence as CO2 bubbles release from suspension.
  equation: 2 C6H8O7 + 3 CaCO3 -> Ca3(C6H5O7)2 + 3 H2O + 3 CO2
  effectId: effervescence_co2
  safetyNotes: Use open vessel and standard eye protection.
  educationalOutcome: Illustrates organic acid reaction with mineral carbonate.
